A||||5||Standard||I got a kill! Woohoo!||||1||
Z||000000||Standard||09-05-2000||05:44 PM||||I was out shoppin' for some items for the GT, and after I left pep boys I was in the right turn lane when I see a camaro come zooming up behind me.. so I take off into the street to see if he wants to play, and sure enough he comes zooming up behind me.  The next light was red and we got the front two spots.  muhahahaha.  I wasn't sure if this was a v6 or lt1 camaro but i figured what the hell.. I looked over at him but he wouldn't look back so I didn't know if he was going to go or not, but as soon as the light turned green and he heard my rev's shoot up he got on the throttle quick.  I saw his nose rise up but if I wanted to see anything else I would have had to look in my rear view mirror  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Only went up to about 50, I had just shifted into 3rd when I shut down.  I pulled him through first and second and it looks like I would have kept pulling away!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  He took the next left and never looked over at me, so I couldn't talk to him... oh well.  Oh yeah, it was a v6 camaro.  looked like 94 or 95.  Those had the 3800, didn't they?  or did they have a 3.4?  <P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT Bastard||09-05-2000||06:27 PM||||3.4, but good kill anyways!  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||09-05-2000||10:07 PM||||It takes a 3.4 Camaro 9 seconds to get to 60 MPH. It takes a v6 fiero 8 seconds.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||09-05-2000||10:49 PM||||Well I'm still happy with it!  My 14 year old 1,100 dollar car can beat up on his new camaro  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I was playing around with what looked like a 70's datsun in really good shape later today.  Never got a chance to line up but it seemed like that car had some balls.  <P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000004||Greg Piet||09-06-2000||03:50 AM||||I guess it is just here in Las Vegas, but my Stock V6 is pretty good in the stop light derbys against anything but a V8.  I only got nailed by a blue bottle snorting, Wright brothers wing Coffee can boy as far as non V8's go.<P>Now granted I do get passed alot after I let off the gas (more than a few seconds above the speed limit is too  much for me...  I have a clean driving record and want to keep it that way).  Normally after my little stint, I do get alot of challenges to go again...  I just tell them to take it to the track (its much safer!)<P>Now for my shameless plug (RACE HERE ITS LEGAL)!! <A HREF="http://www.scca.org" TARGET=_blank>http://www.scca.org</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Shaun41178||09-07-2000||01:30 PM||||Good kill!  yea I am betting that it was a 3.4 model.  If it was a 3800 it probably would have beat you as they have 200 hp stock and are known to run the qtr mile in about 15.3 or so.<P>3.4 camaros weigh to much for them to be fast as it has a horrible power to weight ratio.  Most run the qtr in the mid-high 16 second range.<P>There is a guy in my neighborhood with a 3.4 camaro but has the Z28 badges on it.  I told him that since he has a Z it might be a close  race with my Fiero.  He then said he had the 3.4 in it and I was like oh well it won't be close then. He didn't really take that as smacktalking but he does want to race me.  I have passed him several times going in the opposite direction but I am not going to take the initiative to race him as I know it won't be close.  I want him to challenge and then get shut down hard.  He always has his girl with him too so that would make it even better.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
